# Finds the first library named in the string (the frontmost token that is a valid open library).
# A token is a run of name characters; everything else (spaces, . ' ( ) / \ < > [ ] , : etc.)
# separates. '$' is treated as a name character. Parallel to $getFirstClassRefFromString.

Calculate startPos as 1
Calculate matchPos as rxpos('[\w$]+',pString,kFalse,kFalse,matchLen) ## first token

While matchPos>0
	Calculate name as mid(pString,startPos+matchPos-1,matchLen) ## the matched token
	
	Set reference ref to $libs.$findname(name).$ref
	If ref<>'' ## valid library → its $lib() resolves to a named library
		Quit method ref ## first valid library wins
	End If
	
	# advance past this token and search the remainder
	Calculate startPos as startPos+matchPos-1+matchLen
	Calculate matchPos as rxpos('[\w$]+',mid(pString,startPos,len(pString)),kFalse,kFalse,matchLen)
End While

Quit method ''